> What information should go on a flier for a new 4+1 program, providing a pathway for Economics BS students to do an Environmental Economics Masters degree?
**assistant**:
> For a flier, aim to answer three questions fast: **What is it? Why should I care? How do I start?** Here’s what I’d include.
> 
> ## Essential flier content
> 
> ### 1. Clear headline
> Example:
> 
> **Earn a BS in Economics + MS in Environmental Economics in 5 Years**  
> **New 4+1 Pathway for Economics Majors**
> 
> ### 2. Short program description
> A 1–2 sentence explanation:
> 
> > The 4+1 pathway allows qualified Economics BS students to begin graduate coursework during their senior year and complete a Master’s in Environmental Economics with one additional year of study.
> 
> ### 3. Why students should consider it
> Use concise benefit bullets:
> 
> - Complete two degrees in less time
> - Save tuition by double-counting eligible credits
> - Build expertise in climate, energy, natural resources, sustainability, and policy
> - Strengthen preparation for careers in government, consulting, nonprofits, research, and industry
> - Gain quantitative and policy skills for addressing environmental challenges
> 
> ### 4. Who is eligible
> Include whatever applies:
> 
> - Current Economics BS students
> - Minimum GPA requirement
> - Required prerequisite courses
> - Recommended year to apply, likely junior year
> - Any application requirements: statement, transcript, recommendation, advising meeting
> 
> If details are still pending, say:
> 
> > Open to qualified Economics BS students. Students should meet with an advisor by junior year to plan coursework.
> 
> ### 5. How the pathway works
> A simple visual timeline is ideal:
> 
> **Years 1–3:** Complete Economics BS foundations and prerequisites  
> **Year 4:** Take selected graduate Environmental Economics courses  
> **Year 5:** Complete remaining MS requirements
> 
> You might add:
> 
> > Up to [X] graduate credits may count toward both degrees, subject to approval.
> 
> ### 6. Example topics or courses
> This helps students picture the degree:
> 
> - Environmental and natural resource economics
> - Climate policy and carbon markets
> - Benefit-cost analysis
> - Energy economics
> - Econometrics and data analysis
> - Sustainable development and public policy
> 
> ### 7. Career outcomes
> Include concrete pathways:
> 
> **Career paths include:**
> 
> - Environmental or energy analyst
> - Policy analyst
> - Sustainability consultant
> - Climate risk analyst
> - Research associate
> - Government or NGO program analyst
> - Preparation for PhD study or advanced policy work
> 
> ### 8. Call to action
> Make this highly visible:
> 
> **Interested? Talk to your Economics advisor today.**  
> Contact: **[Name, email, office]**  
> Program page: **[URL]**  
> Info session: **[date/time/location]**  
> QR code: **Apply / Learn More**
> 
> ## Optional but valuable additions
> 
> - Application deadline
> - “No GRE required,” if true
> - Scholarship or assistantship opportunities
> - Testimonial from a student or faculty member
> - Faculty contact names
> - Logos for departments/programs
> - A small “Is this right for me?” box:
> 
> > This program is a great fit if you are interested in economics, data, policy, climate change, sustainability, or environmental decision-making.
> 
> A strong flier should be visually simple: headline, 3–5 benefits, timeline, eligibility, and a bold contact/QR code.
