> 2. Bachelor of Science – Economics (BS-ECON) 
> The Bachelor of Science in Economics degree requires 120 credits, including all university  requirements, major requirements, and related coursework. 
> The Economics major requirements (54 cr - minimum) include: 
> Core Courses (18 cr) 
> ● ECON 101 – Introduction to Microeconomics (3 cr) 
> ● ECON 103 – Introduction to Macroeconomics (3 cr) 
> ● ECON 301 – Quantitative Microeconomic Theory (3 cr) 
> ● ECON 304 – Quantitative Macroeconomic Theory (3 cr) 
> ● ECON 306 – Introduction to Econometrics (3 cr) 
