> PART IV. ASSESSMENT PLAN 
> The BS-ECON-MEE program will be assessed according to the learning goals for the BS-ECON and MEE programs. No unique assessments are expected for the BS-ECON-MEE program. 
> PART V. FINANCIAL AID 
> BS-ECON-MEE students are eligible for all degree-appropriate financial aid, including the  possibility of graduate assistantships during the 5th year. No unique financial aid is expected for  the BS-ECON-MEE program. 
> PART VI. DEPARTMENTAL OPERATIONS 
> BS-ECON-MEE students must follow all expectations of students in both the ECON and MEE  programs, which include expectations from the Department of Economics, the Lerner College  of Business and Economics, the School of Marine Science & Policy, and the university at large. Any questions should be directed to the MEE program director or School of Marine Science & Policy administrative staff.
